ANTHROPIC
=F0=9F=8E=AC Anthropic punches up with Claude Opus 5
Image source: Anthropic
The Rundown: Anthropic just released Claude Opus 5 across the Claude apps,
Claude Code, and the API, describing it as a =E2=80=9Cthoughtful and proact=
ive=E2=80=9D AI
that nears the intelligence of its Fable 5 model at half the price.
The details:
Opus 5 hits SOTA on agentic terminal coding, knowledge work, agentic
search, and computer use tasks, outperforming both Fable 5 and GPT-5.6
Sol.
On ARC-AGI-3, it hit 30.2%, 3x as high as the next best model, also
ranking #1 on Artificial Analysis=E2=80=99 Intelligence Index leaderboard.
Anthropic ran the new model on International Math Olympiad 2026 problems,
where it scored 42 out of 42, well past the 29-point gold threshold.
The company describes it as its most aligned AI, noting that it matches
Mythos 5 at finding software bugs but stays well behind it at writing
exploits.
Why it matters: This is Anthropic filling Fable gaps with what it does
best: offering intelligence from a tier above at a far lower price. So
far, it=E2=80=99s been Sonnet matching Opus. Now, it=E2=80=99s Opus matchin=
g Fable at $5
and $25 per million tokens (same as 4.8), giving people who won=E2=80=99t p=
ay
Fable rates a reliable and powerful option to work with.
