OPEN SOURCE AI
=F0=9F=9B=A1 Industry giants unite to protect open models
Image source: Jensen Huang / X
The Rundown: Nvidia, Microsoft, Meta, and 47 other tech companies, VCs,
and nonprofits just signed an open letter urging Washington not to
restrict open-weight AI models =E2=80=94 giving a bunch of reasons why it=
=E2=80=99s
crucial to U.S. AI leadership.
The details:
Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang first shared the letter, his first post on X, with
25 signatories but a few crucial ones missing, including OpenAI.
In a day, the letter garnered widespread support, with signatories
doubling as OpenAI, Google, AMD, Cisco, and others joined =E2=80=94 but not
Anthropic.
The letter argues that open weights expand access to the AI economy, keep
competition alive, broaden cyber defense, and help avoid vendor lock-in.
It also notes that distillation should not be confused with
misappropriation and calls to avoid premature restrictions that push AI
innovation overseas.
Why it matters: The letter comes amid accusations that Chinese labs
extracted intelligence from U.S. models, including Anthropic=E2=80=99s Fabl=
e.
Washington=E2=80=99s response remains unclear, but the pressure is on the l=
one
U.S. frontier lab off the list, the one to gain most from a crackdown. And
people are already asking for answers.
